{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_3>\n__author__ = 'MoonBall'\n\nimport sys\n# sys.stdin = open('data/D.in', 'r')\nT = 1\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef main():\n    P, K = map(int, input().split())\n    \n    if K == 0:\n        print(pow(P, P - 1, MOD))\n        return\n    \n    # Build the functional graph: x -> (K*x) % P\n    next_node = [K * i % P for i in range(P)]\n    \n    # Detect cycles and count their frequencies\n    seen = [False] * P\n    cycle_counter = [0] * P\n    \n    for i in range(P):\n        if seen[i]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Trace the path until we find a visited node\n        path = []\n        cur = i\n        while not seen[cur]:\n            seen[cur] = True\n            path.append(cur)\n            cur = next_node[cur]\n        \n        # Find where the cycle starts\n        try:\n            idx = path.index(cur)\n            cycle_len = len(path) - idx\n        except ValueError:\n            cycle_len = 1\n        \n        cycle_counter[cycle_len] += 1\n    \n    # Compute the result\n    res = 1\n    for cl in range(1, P):\n        if cycle_counter[cl] == 0:\n            continue\n        \n        eff = cl * cycle_counter[cl]\n        if cl > 1:\n            eff += cycle_counter[1]\n        \n        res = (res * pow(eff, cycle_counter[cl], MOD)) % MOD\n    \n    print(res)\n\nfor _ in range(T):\n    main()\n</your_rewritten_code_3>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static final long MOD = 1000000007;\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int T = 1;\n        for (int t = 0; t < T; t++) {\n            solve(sc);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    static void solve(Scanner sc) {\n        int P = sc.nextInt();\n        int K = sc.nextInt();\n        \n        if (K == 0) {\n            System.out.println(modPow(P, P - 1, MOD));\n            return;\n        }\n        \n        // Build the functional graph: x -> (K*x) % P\n        int[] nextNode = new int[P];\n        for (int i = 0; i < P; i++) {\n            nextNode[i] = (int)((long)K * i % P);\n        }\n        \n        // Detect cycles and count their frequencies\n        boolean[] seen = new boolean[P];\n        int[] cycleCounter = new int[P];\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < P; i++) {\n            if (seen[i]) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            \n            // Trace the path until we find a visited node\n            List<Integer> path = new ArrayList<>();\n            int cur = i;\n            while (!seen[cur]) {\n                seen[cur] = true;\n                path.add(cur);\n                cur = nextNode[cur];\n            }\n            \n            // Find where the cycle starts\n            int idx = path.indexOf(cur);\n            int cycleLen;\n            if (idx == -1) {\n                cycleLen = 1;\n            } else {\n                cycleLen = path.size() - idx;\n            }\n            \n            cycleCounter[cycleLen]++;\n        }\n        \n        // Compute the result\n        long res = 1;\n        for (int cl = 1; cl < P; cl++) {\n            if (cycleCounter[cl] == 0) {\n                continue;\n            }\n            \n            long eff = (long)cl * cycleCounter[cl];\n            if (cl > 1) {\n                eff += cycleCounter[1];\n            }\n            \n            res = (res * modPow(eff, cycleCounter[cl], MOD)) % MOD;\n        }\n        \n        System.out.println(res);\n    }\n    \n    static long modPow(long base, long exp, long mod) {\n        long result = 1;\n        base %= mod;\n        while (exp > 0) {\n            if ((exp & 1) == 1) {\n                result = (result * base) % mod;\n            }\n            base = (base * base) % mod;\n            exp >>= 1;\n        }\n        return result;\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-8.034383063204587e-05, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.0005727558163926005, -3.2066785934148356e-05, -0.07897060364484787, -0.16348132491111755, -1.156323378381785e-05, -3.099436753473128e-06, -9.727005090098828e-05, -0.078892283141613, -0.0015026956098154187, -0.5837631225585938, -0.00013529339048545808, -0.014204702340066433, -2.622600959512056e-06, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -5.364403477869928e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -8.344646857949556e-07, 0.0, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -5.006777428206988e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.5603137016296387, -0.3132684528827667, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.002891884883865714, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -0.005929854232817888, -4.768370445162873e-07, -9.65590606938349e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.729855441430118e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -5.8412379075889476e-06, -2.264974000354414e-06, -7.295342220459133e-05, -0.0623767226934433, -5.602820692729438e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -9.059865078597795e-06, -6.437280717364047e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07